module display_synth.neg_1

// THE GATE MUST KEEP GATING: the fields are exactly the ones `pos_1` prints
// perfectly well, and the ONLY difference is the missing `#impl(Display)`. The
// slot is refused all the same.
//
// This is the cell that stops the synthesis from being an improvement that
// quietly repeals a rule. D186's gate semantics make bare interpolation require
// the TYPE AUTHOR's opt-in; a synthesis that fired without the gate would print
// something reasonable, pass every byte comparison against nothing, and leave
// the opt-in meaning nothing at all. A gate that stopped gating would make the
// whole acceptance false while every green tick stayed green.
//
// BOTH SIDES REFUSE THIS, measured 2026-09-18, which is why it is a `neg_` and
// not a subset lag: the oracle answers `E_INTERP_NO_DISPLAY` -- the diagnostic
// D186 names for exactly this -- and novac answers with its own subset refusal
// at the slot. The differential judges `pos_*` files only, so this file asserts
// novac's refusal rather than an agreement between the two.

type Bare {
    x int
    y int
}

fn main() {
    ro b = Bare{ x: 1, y: 2 }
    println("${b}")
}
